            "review_title": "Review at NOIRE Dining & Cafe - Pham Ngoc Thach",
            "review_text": "Dingo_6152\nFremantle, Australia3911 contributions\n0\nStill finding their identity\nNov 2025 • Couples\nFor our last night in Ho Chi Minh City we were looking for somewhere close to our hotel and I’d passed by Noire numerous times so we’d thought we give it a try. \n\nIt’s relatively new establishment, only open a month, so there’s not many reviews to go by. It is certainly very modern and flashy. Initially we were going to eat outdoors in the alfresco area but they had some private function and the noise from the band was overwhelming. Luckily inside was relatively soundproof. The only diners inside seemed more interested in instagramming the decor than actually eating. At times they were intrusive but management didn’t seem to mind. \n\nThe menu is dominated by western dishes and we went with the surf & turf platter. The seafood was grilled perfectly. The cocktails were nicely balanced. Service was efficient.\n\nI think that conceptually the idea of European style cafe provides a different atmosphere from many of the other nearby restaurants. The food for a westerner however does not really push the boundaries but it’s good quality. I feel like they are still finding their identity and there is room to grow.\nRead more\nWritten December 31, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
